The "neoGFX" C++ app/game engine and development platform is built with CMake (3.24 or later).

neoGFX depends on the following, found by CMake in the install prefix (default /usr/local) or via CMAKE_PREFIX_PATH:

* neolib (CMake package; brings in Boost, OpenSSL and zlib)
* FreeType (CMake package, or headers and library)
* HarfBuzz (CMake package, or headers and library)
* libjpeg-turbo (static library jpeg-static, else any libjpeg)
* Vulkan SDK, including shaderc (found via the VULKAN_SDK environment variable set by the SDK installer); shaderc_shared.dll must be on PATH, or shipped next to the program, to use the Vulkan renderer (both it and vulkan-1.dll are delay loaded, so a program without them still runs with OpenGL)
* GLEW and libpng: the prebuilt static libraries in 3rdparty/lib and the headers in 3rdparty
* libssh (CMake package), for Design Studio's default element library

Build and install (Windows, from a Visual Studio developer prompt):

  cmake -S . -B out
  cmake --build out --config Release
  cmake --install out --config Release

Windows builds use the static C runtime (/MT, /MTd), as neolib does.
The install prefix defaults to /usr/local; set CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX to change it.
Programs and the plugins they load (.nrl, .nel, .plg) are built into out/bin (out/bin/<config> with Visual Studio generators) and installed into <prefix>/bin.
The example apps are installed into <prefix>/share/neogfx/examples and the GUI test app into <prefix>/share/neogfx/test.

Options (default):

* NEOGFX_BUILD_DESIGN_STUDIO (ON): neoGFX Design Studio and its default element library
* NEOGFX_BUILD_NEOS_ELEMENT_LIBRARY (OFF): Design Studio's neos element library (needs neos: CMake package, or headers and library)
* NEOGFX_BUILD_WEB_VIEW_PLUGIN (OFF): the web_view plugin and neogfx_cef (needs CEF)
* NEOGFX_BUILD_TESTS (ON): the GUI test app
* NEOGFX_BUILD_EXAMPLES (OFF): the example apps (video_poker, chess, mod_tracker)
* NEOGFX_DEBUG (ON): defines NEOGFX_DEBUG
* NEOGFX_BUILD_CORES (empty): number of cores for concurrent compilation; empty or 0 uses all cores
  (Visual Studio: /MP<n>; Ninja: a compile job pool; Makefiles: use cmake --build -j <n>)

Using an installed neoGFX:

  find_package(neogfx REQUIRED)
  target_link_libraries(myapp PRIVATE neogfx::neogfx)
  neogfx_add_resources(myapp src/myapp.nrc)
